<h1>Alchemeow</h1>
<p class="standfirst">Sound design &amp; implementation <span class="ph">&middot; [2025] &middot; [team or studio name]</span></p>

<h2>Project overview</h2>
<!-- PLACEHOLDER -->
<div class="ph">
  <p>Alchemeow is a cosy potion-brewing puzzle game about a cat who inherits an alchemist's workshop. Players combine ingredients, tend bubbling cauldrons and try very hard not to blow anything up.</p>
  <p>The sound needed to be warm, tactile and a little bit silly: lots of glass, liquid and wood, and a cat with opinions.</p>
</div>

<h2>My role</h2>
<!-- PLACEHOLDER -->
<div class="ph">
  <ul>
    <li>Sound designer and audio implementer</li>
    <li>Foley recording: glassware, liquids, dried herbs and wooden tools</li>
    <li>Cat vocals, recorded and edited from [source]</li>
    <li>Implementation in FMOD Studio and Unity, including adaptive music layers (music by [composer])</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<h2>Technical approach</h2>
<!-- PLACEHOLDER -->
<div class="ph">
  <p>Each ingredient has its own pour, plop and fizz. The cauldron is a parameter-driven loop that speeds up and rises in pitch as a potion gets closer to boiling over, so players can hear trouble coming.</p>
  <p>Successful brews trigger short musical stingers written in the key of the current music cue, so every reward sits neatly with the score.</p>
</div>

